status: 500

PDB-REDO has no entry 1STP, and that absence is the point of the fixture set.

MmtfImporter.getFromMmcifUrl is 17 lines, and roughly half of them are the
catch: it prints "WARNING: could not parse" and returns null, and the caller
filters the null out. Mirroring 1STP would leave that half uncovered, so the
pdbredo recipe asks for 1AIE 1STP 2ONX and only two of the three are served.

Probed upstream over https on 2026-09-16 (curl, no proxy):

  GET /db/1stp/1stp_final.cif   500   21 bytes   {"error":"Not Found"}
  GET /db/1pen/1pen_final.cif   500   21 bytes   {"error":"Not Found"}
  GET /db/4hhb/4hhb_final.cif   500   21 bytes   {"error":"Not Found"}
  GET /db/1aie/1aie_final.cif   200   53989 bytes

So 500 -- not 404 -- is what a client asking PDB-REDO for a missing entry
gets. Both statuses reach HttpURLConnection.getInputStream as an IOException
and both are caught identically here, which is precisely why the status has to
be recorded rather than inferred from what the client happens to survive.

The body is not served. Nothing in this tree reads an error body, and a
21-byte payload recorded here would be a second thing to keep true.
